NAMABLE should look normal, since the usual rule is that the E is only needed to maintain a soft C or G sound, as in changeable or replaceable. So we have curable, notable, erasable, but also we have either/ors like liv(e)able and lov(e)able, and of course, NAM(e)ABLE. 

Why?  Because English.

